@startuml proposal-implementation-issue-states
' cumin works - PROPOSAL, not the rule of today: states of an implementation issue, as they could be.
' Differences from today are marked NEW. See the draft pull request for the reasons.
' Render: run scripts/render-diagrams.sh at the root of the repository.

hide empty description

state "Draft (no status label)" as Draft
Draft : do / the Planner or the Owner writes the issue

state "ready" as Ready
Ready : do / wait for a free slot

state "implementing" as Implementing
Implementing : do / the Implementer works

state "awaiting-checks" as Checks
Checks : do / the required checks run

state "reviewing" as Reviewing
Reviewing : do / the Reviewer reviews

state "awaiting-merge-decision  (NEW name)" as OwnerReview
OwnerReview : do / the Owner reviews the pull request

state "merging  (NEW state)" as Merging
Merging : do / cumin merges, then closes the issue

state "awaiting-owner-decision" as Decision
Decision : do / the Owner answers

[*] --> Draft
Draft --> Ready : the Owner adds ready
Ready --> Implementing : [ready is the Owner's, blockers closed,\nslot free]\n/ request the implementation
Implementing --> Checks : [no agent runs, pull request verified]\n/ add the closing link
Implementing --> Implementing : [no agent runs, no verified pull request,\nfirst time]\n/ request the Implementer again  (NEW)
Implementing --> Decision : [no agent runs, and: a question of the\nImplementer, or the second time]\n/ notify the Owner
Checks --> Reviewing : [required checks passed]\n/ request the review
Checks --> Implementing : [a required check failed,\nfix requests under the limit]\n/ request a check fix
Checks --> Decision : [a required check failed, fix requests\nat the limit; or no result in time]\n/ notify the Owner
Checks --> Implementing : [pull request conflicts]\n/ request a conflict resolution
Reviewing --> Implementing : [no agent runs, changes requested on\nthe head commit, rounds under the limit]\n/ request a review fix
Reviewing --> Merging : [no agent runs, approved on the head commit,\nchecks passed, risk/low]  (NEW target)
Reviewing --> OwnerReview : [no agent runs, approved on the head commit,\nchecks passed, risk/medium or risk/high]\n/ notify the Owner
Reviewing --> Checks : [no agent runs, head commit moved,\nor a check does not pass]
Reviewing --> Reviewing : [no agent runs, no review on the\nhead commit, first time]\n/ request the review again
Reviewing --> Decision : [no agent runs, and: rounds at the limit,\na question of the Reviewer, or the second time]\n/ notify the Owner
OwnerReview --> Merging : [the Owner approved the head commit,\nchecks passed]  (NEW target)
OwnerReview --> Implementing : [the Owner requested changes]\n/ request a response
OwnerReview --> Implementing : [pull request conflicts]\n/ request a conflict resolution
OwnerReview --> Ready : the Owner adds ready
Merging --> [*] : [pull request merged]\n/ close the issue, write the follow-up note
Merging --> Implementing : [merge refused: conflict]\n/ request a conflict resolution
Merging --> Decision : [merge refused for another lasting reason]\n/ notify the Owner
Decision --> Ready : the Owner adds ready

legend right
  PROPOSAL. A box is a state: a label on GitHub (written without "cumin/status/").
  Every guard reads only facts on GitHub and "no agent of cumin runs for this issue".
  No arrow needs the event "the run ended": a restart of cumin loses nothing.
  "merging" makes a merge whose answer was lost visible: the next poll reads whether the pull request is merged.
endlegend

@enduml
